NAME
    pkg - package manager (install, remove, and run TOS packages)

SYNOPSIS
    pkg list
    pkg search
    pkg info <name>
    pkg install [<name> [--key <licenseKey>] | <dir>]
    pkg make-disk <mount> [name ...]
    pkg uninstall <name>

    install <name>          shortcut for 'pkg install <name>'
    uninstall <name>        shortcut for 'pkg uninstall <name>'

DESCRIPTION
    pkg is the single package system in TOS (the legacy "module manager" was
    retired in v1.3.1; 'mod' is now an alias for pkg). It installs add-ons,
    resolves their dependencies, verifies integrity, and dispatches the shell
    commands they provide.

    Sources: a package is a directory containing a package.lua manifest plus its
    files. pkg reads native package.lua, OPPM-style package.oppm.lua, and bundled
    Optional Utilities disks. install/uninstall/enable require an ADMIN session.

    Security:
      * Writes are confined to /usr and /var/pkg. A kind="service" package may
        also install ONE /etc/rc.d/<file>.lua and ONE /etc/<name>.cfg — nothing
        else under /etc, and never /tos or /init.lua.
      * When a manifest declares hashes, every file is SHA-256 verified
        (constant-time) before it is written.
      * A package command runs in a capability sandbox built from the manifest's
        declared, ALLOWLISTED capabilities. The "legacy" capability (raw os/io)
        can never be requested by a manifest.

SUBCOMMANDS
    list           Installed packages and their enabled state.
    search         Packages available in any repo or mounted disk.
    info <name>    Manifest details: version, kind, deps, capabilities.
    install [arg]  One smart verb. A bare NAME resolves dependencies and
                   installs from any known source. A PATH (anything with a
                   "/") installs that single package directory explicitly.
                   NO argument scans every mounted disk and prompts before
                   installing each package it finds. (The old 'install-dir'
                   and 'from-floppy' still work as hidden aliases.)
    make-disk <mount> [name ...]
                   Build an Optional Utilities disk from your INSTALLED add-ons
                   (parity with `deploy`, which builds a whole-OS image). Emits
                   one package dir per add-on plus a self-contained picker
                   install.lua, so the disk installs on any TOS machine with no
                   dev box. Name args limit the export; omit for all add-ons.
                   Targets removable media only (system paths are refused).
    uninstall <name>   Remove an installed package.

EXAMPLES
    pkg search
    pkg install tetris          (by name)   or:  install tetris
    pkg install                 (scan the inserted Optional Utilities disk)
    pkg info tape

ERRORS
    "Insufficient privileges: admin required"   You are not ADMIN+.
    "already installed (uninstall first): X"     Remove X before reinstalling.
    "hash mismatch on <file>"                    The package failed integrity
                                                 verification; install aborted.
    "package not found in any repo: X"           No source provides X.

SEE ALSO
